{
  "_comment": [
    "Central source of truth for per-agent model selection.",
    "",
    "Copy to .claude/agent-models.json to opt in. Without this file,",
    "scripts/sync-agent-models.mjs is a no-op.",
    "",
    "Use Claude Code's short-form aliases, never dated model IDs. An alias",
    "tracks the current generation, so a model upgrade needs no edit here and",
    "no agent silently pins to a retired version:",
    "  - 'sonnet'  (default, balanced)",
    "  - 'opus'    (deep reasoning: planning and final judgment only)",
    "  - 'haiku'   (fast read-only lookup and scanning)",
    "  - 'inherit' (use the parent session's model)",
    "",
    "Dated IDs (claude-opus-5, claude-sonnet-5) belong only in application",
    "code and API examples, where the alias is not a valid model identifier.",
    "",
    "Opus is reserved for the design chain — `architect`, `planner`, `judge`.",
    "See CLAUDE.md Agent Routing. Routing a fourth agent to opus is a cost",
    "decision: opus runs roughly 15-20x haiku and 3-5x sonnet per token, which",
    "erases the cost advantage of delegating to a subagent at all.",
    "",
    "Agents not listed under `agents` take default.model.",
    "",
    "After editing, run: node scripts/sync-agent-models.mjs",
    "In CI, verify with:  node scripts/sync-agent-models.mjs --check"
  ],

  "default": { "model": "sonnet" },

  "agents": {
    "architect":           { "model": "opus" },
    "planner":             { "model": "opus" },
    "judge":               { "model": "opus" },
    "codebase-researcher": { "model": "haiku" },
    "perf-auditor":        { "model": "haiku" }
  }
}
